# 2026-08-25 (security-review): Claude Code's per-project state includes
# permission rules with baked-in bearer tokens in curl commands.  A live
# Vapi token leaked via .claude/settings.local.json during a codebase
# bundle for audit; excluding here at the git layer is the same fix at
# a different boundary.
#
# 2026-08-29: switched from blanket `.claude/` to per-entry rules so
# SHARED team plugins under `.claude/plugins/` can be version-controlled
# while per-user settings + local permission rules + bearer-token leak
# vectors stay ignored.  Git rule: to include ANYTHING inside a
# gitignored directory you must first un-ignore the directory itself,
# then re-ignore the specific children you want to keep out.
.claude/*
# ignore the risky per-user + local-permission files by name
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/mcp*.json
.claude/session*.json
.claude/cache/
.claude/logs/
.claude/*.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks*
# but DO track the shared plugins directory
!.claude/plugins/

# NOTE: .github/workflows/ is NOT ignored — CI + auto-deploy workflows
# live there and must be version-controlled.  A prior version of this
# file ignored the whole directory; removed 2026-08-25 so GitHub Actions
# picks up deploy-lightsail.yml.  If a workflow ever needs a secret it
# must come from GitHub repo Secrets (Settings → Secrets), never from
# a file committed to the repo.
